WEBVTT

00:00.600 --> 00:03.982
Two pendulums. One swings five degrees…

00:04.002 --> 00:05.672
the other, fifteen.

00:05.770 --> 00:08.334
Which one finishes ten swings FIRST?

00:09.490 --> 00:11.479
Most people pick one of them.

00:12.660 --> 00:13.585
Watch.

00:15.780 --> 00:17.876
They finish… together!

00:18.940 --> 00:23.414
The period T equals two pi root L over g has no

00:23.434 --> 00:24.797
amplitude in it.

00:24.817 --> 00:26.477
And no mass.

00:26.707 --> 00:28.537
The bigger swing goes farther…

00:28.557 --> 00:30.787
but it also moves faster.

00:32.167 --> 00:36.796
Now, a spring. At the extreme, the block stops for just an

00:36.816 --> 00:37.726
instant.

00:38.187 --> 00:40.941
But its acceleration is NOT zero.

00:40.961 --> 00:42.901
It's the largest it ever gets…

00:42.921 --> 00:45.391
and it points straight back to the mean.

00:46.638 --> 00:50.375
As it swings, potential energy turns into kinetic energy…

00:50.395 --> 00:53.678
and back again. The total never changes.

00:55.401 --> 01:00.261
LearnLoop AI. Predict. Watch. Explain.
